# Exporting jobs from an HP DFE
1. Move all jobs on the one you are exporting from to the Press Controller
  - If this is not done, you won't be able to one-click export all. Anything that is in the held queue or print queue will not allow you to export them
  - If there are any errored jobs, ripping jobs, or pending jobs, it will not let you export these jobs as well
2. Once all jobs are selected, right-click > Export> Save to \\192.168.1.{{DFEIP}}\Jobs\Exported
  - This will speed the exporting process up by saving locally on the DFE instead of your PC

### There are two ways to continue: 1. Resending the batches within SiteFlow or 2. Import all of the jobs into the other DFE.
#### Downsides of 1.
    - Takes a while to resend all batches
    - Multiple UIs to go through each event to resend batches
    - Have to be extremely careful not to delete a job you haven't sent yet within the Mounted Folder
#### Downsides of 2.
    - Reliant on internet speed
    - Reliant on HP Software
      - Sometimes the imported jobs hit 100%, but don't upload. This happens a lot, so I usually stick to less than 50 jobs and under 1 GB
        - You can upload 50 jobs at once and upload 50 after they are completed is the best option
    - Causes a slowdown on the DFE you are importing to

